mympd/25.3.0@ohpcd/stable: Apply patch (portability): 0001 tests: route the unit test scratch directory (init/clean of the test environment, workdir global, certificate cleanup, filehandler/list/state/http-cache test paths) through a TMPDIR-aware test_tmpdir()/test_tmpfile() helper, and clean the tree with an in-process nftw() recursion instead of system("rm -rf"), so the upstream suite runs on HarmonyOS/OHOS where /tmp is a read-only mount; with TMPDIR unset this resolves to the upstream hardcoded /tmp/mympd-test path, so other platforms are behaviour-equivalent
mympd/25.3.0@ohpcd/stable: Apply patch (portability): 0003 build: build.sh is driven from CMake through execute_process() in three places (create assets, copy assets, generate html documentation). On platforms without binfmt_script support a script file cannot be executed directly, so a bash/sh interpreter is located at configure time (find_program) and the script is invoked through it (a no-op change on platforms where direct execution already works)
mympd/25.3.0@ohpcd/stable: Apply patch (portability): 0004 tests: the unit_test target materializes test/testfiles below the build tree with cmake -E create_symlink before building. Symlink creation is denied on the platform (EPERM across the filesystem), so the directory is materialized as a real copy instead (cmake -E rm -r -f + copy_directory); identical content, no symlink involved
mympd/25.3.0@ohpcd/stable: Apply patch (portability): 0005 TLS: find_ca_cert_store() probes a fixed list of system CA bundle locations (openSUSE, Fedora and Debian layouts) and finds none on HarmonyOS PC, whose system store lives at /etc/ssl/certs/cacert.pem; the HarmonyOS location is appended to the probe list (a no-op on platforms where that path does not exist)
mympd/25.3.0@ohpcd/stable: Apply patch (portability): 0006 tests: test_http_client fetches README.md from raw.githubusercontent.com, which the verification network does not reach (name resolution succeeds, the TCP connect fails); the request is repointed at the byte-identical file through the gh-proxy.com mirror prefix so the network test still exercises the same fetch and TLS path on the verification host (a no-op change on networks with direct access)
mympd/25.3.0@ohpcd/stable: Apply patch (bugfix): 0007 options: the long_options[] array passed to getopt_long() ends without the all-zero terminating entry that the getopt(3) contract requires. An exact match or a short option is served before the scan needs the terminator, but an unmatched long option or an unambiguous abbreviation keeps the scan walking past the array into unrelated memory (on the platform libc this is a deterministic out-of-bounds read: device-verified SIGSEGV, exit 139, for both --foo and --dum, while --dump and -Z stay clean). The terminator puts the scan back inside the array; the option table itself is unchanged and the fix is correct on every libc
mympd/25.3.0@ohpcd/stable: Apply patch (portability): 0008 files: main() sets umask(0077), so the 0770 mkdir in testdir() - the single directory-creation point of the whole tree (work, cache, config, state, ssl, cover/thumbnail caches) - stores mode 2700 on HarmonyOS PC storage, where the group bits are what every later access below a directory is resolved through and chmod() after creation is ignored. Such a directory then rejects entry for everyone, its owner included, and the whole bootstrap fails with EACCES (device-verified with a minimal reproducer). The umask is cleared around the mkdir call and restored immediately after, so the requested group-accessible 0770 mode survives; OHOS-only, guarded by the MYMPD_OHOS define that the recipe adds for OHOS builds, other platforms keep the upstream behaviour unchanged
